  "problem": "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(a-x)^{2}-a, & x\\ne -3, \\\\ 9, & x=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-3,$ **in ascending order**, what are the possible values of $a?$\n\n$a=$ \n{{field-1}}\nor\n$a=$ \n{{field-2}}",
